      "title": "Pressure release creates micro-bubbles",
      "description": "Part of the clarified water is pumped to the saturator at about 4–6 bar, where air dissolves into it (Henry's law: more gas dissolves at higher pressure). At the release valve the pressure drops to atmospheric and the excess air comes out of solution as micro-bubbles, which attach to flocs and float them to the surface.",
