  "summary": "A dissolved air flotation (DAF) unit removes suspended solids, oil and grease from water. Part of the clarified water is pressurised and saturated with air; when the pressure is released in the tank, micro-bubbles form and float the flocs to the surface, where a skimmer removes them as sludge.",
